How to Use This Guide
Use this document as the implementation runbook for the frontend. Build phases in order, validate each phase against the backend contract, and do not implement financial authorization or accounting logic in the browser.
Core rule
The backend is authoritative for identity, ownership, balances, limits, risk decisions, transfer state, ledger postings, and final transaction outcome. The frontend collects input, invokes APIs, and renders verified backend state.

