Executive Summary
NovaBank is a production-style retail banking web application designed to sit directly above the existing banking API. The interface adopts the restrained visual language of the supplied Haven reference while replacing marketing-oriented composition with operational banking workflows. The first release focuses on authentication, dashboard, accounts, account details, funds transfer, transaction history, transaction detail, profile and logout. Additional modules such as beneficiaries, payments, cards, statements, notifications and security controls are introduced only where matching backend services exist.
•	Critical money movement uses a Review → Submit → Result flow.
•	Every logical transfer carries an idempotency key to prevent duplicate processing.
•	Pending, processing, under-review, rejected, failed and completed states are rendered from backend status—not inferred by the UI.
•	Available balance and current balance are presented separately and never recomputed in the browser.
•	Keycloak uses Authorization Code Flow with PKCE; no client secret is embedded in the SPA.
•	All critical flows include negative, rollback, authorization and duplicate-submit tests.
•	The design targets WCAG 2.2 AA and production-style browser security controls.
 
PART I – ARCHITECTURE & UX DESIGN
1. Objectives and Scope
•	Provide a modern banking UI integrated with the existing Spring Boot REST services.
•	Support authenticated customer access through Keycloak and JWT access tokens.
•	Expose accounts, balances, transaction history and transfer functions safely.
•	Provide clear operational feedback for loading, pending, success, failure and access-denied conditions.
•	Remain responsive across desktop, tablet and mobile.
•	Keep financial business rules and authorization on the server.
•	Establish an implementation path that can later move from AWS VM-based lab infrastructure to Kubernetes.
