Contract validation
Before coding each feature, compare its TypeScript model against the backend DTO / OpenAPI contract. Do not hand-invent field names or enums.

21. API Client Behavior
•	Single base URL from environment configuration.
•	Attach current bearer token to authenticated requests.
•	Attach or preserve X-Correlation-ID where supported.
•	Never log Authorization headers or raw access tokens.
•	Normalize safe API errors into a common UI error model.
•	Do not automatically retry POST transfer requests unless the same logical operation preserves the same idempotency key.
22. HTTP and Error Handling
HTTP	Expected UI behavior
200	Render successful response
201	Render newly created resource
202	Render pending/processing state
400	Show safe request validation errors
401	Reauthenticate / session-expired flow
403	Access denied; do not leak resource data
404	Resource not found or no longer available
409	Conflict / idempotency / concurrent state conflict
422	Business validation such as insufficient funds when backend uses 422
429	Rate-limited; explain retry behavior
500	Generic service error with correlation/reference ID
503	Service temporarily unavailable

The exact status-code contract must be verified against the implemented backend before release.
23. Recommended Backend Error Contract
{
  "timestamp": "2026-09-25T14:15:00Z",
  "status": 422,
  "code": "INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS",
  "message": "Insufficient available balance",
  "correlationId": "87ed..."
}
Use machine-readable code for UI branching and a backend-approved message for user-visible text. Never expose Oracle errors, Java stack traces or internal class names.
24. Money and Currency Rules
•	Do not recompute authoritative balances in JavaScript.
•	Use backend-returned monetary values and explicit currency codes.
•	Use Intl.NumberFormat for localized display.
•	Avoid floating-point business calculations in the UI.
•	The backend remains authoritative for fees, exchange rates, rounding and settlement values.
25. Idempotency and Duplicate Submission
Generate a unique identifier for the logical transfer before the POST and preserve it until the final outcome is known.
const idempotencyKey = crypto.randomUUID();

POST /api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
Idempotency-Key: <same key for the same logical attempt>
•	Disable the Confirm Transfer button immediately after submit.
•	Show a processing state.
•	Do not generate a new idempotency key for an automatic retry of the same logical transfer.
•	If the browser loses the response, query the transfer by returned/known reference where supported before encouraging another submit.
