36. Critical End-to-End Test Cases
Scenario	Expected result
Successful internal transfer	Backend commits balances, ledger, transfer and outbox; UI shows verified status.
Insufficient funds	No unauthorized debit; safe business error shown.
Same source/destination	Rejected according to backend validation.
Unauthorized source account	403/secure denial; no account data leaked.
Duplicate submit	Same idempotency key returns same logical result; no duplicate money movement.
Expired token	Reauthentication/session flow; no transaction submitted with invalid session.
Risk review	UI shows UNDER_REVIEW/PENDING rather than success.
Risk rejection	UI shows rejected state and safe reason if supplied.
API timeout after submit	Do not blindly resubmit; reconcile using transfer/status lookup when available.
Second balance update fails	Database rolls back; no partial success exposed.
Kafka unavailable	Transfer behavior follows outbox design; DB commit must not depend on direct Kafka publish if outbox pattern is correctly implemented.

37. Database Consistency Validation
For an internal transfer of 100 from A=1000 to B=500:
Validation	Expected
Source available/current balance	Reduced according to backend rules
Destination balance	Increased according to backend rules
Version columns	Incremented where optimistic concurrency/versioning is used
Transfer row	Created once
Ledger	Balanced debit and credit entries
Outbox	One committed event for the transfer
UI	Matches backend transfer and account state after refresh/requery

38. Observability
